Pulse — Licensing Overview
==========================

Copyright (c) 2026 Oblivion Pictures — Michael de Meyer (https://howispulse.com)

Pulse is source-available, not open source. The source is published so that
anyone can read and audit it. Reading is permitted; reusing is not. You may not
modify Pulse or redistribute it, and you may not take code from it into another
project. Two licences apply, depending on which part of the repository a file
belongs to.


1. Server components — Pulse Server License 1.0
------------------------------------------------
Full text: LICENSE-SERVER.md

    services/
    shared/
    infra/
    Dockerfile.service
    docker-compose.yml
    pyproject.toml
    uv.lock

These are the components required to operate a Pulse server. You may evaluate
them for up to 32 consecutive days, and you may read their source at any time.
Operating a Pulse server beyond the trial period requires a commercial licence
from the copyright holder, regardless of whether the deployment is commercial,
private or non-profit. Modification and redistribution are not permitted at any
time.

Self-hosting is offered as a paid, activated service. See
https://howispulse.com for terms.


2. Client components — Pulse Client License 1.0
-----------------------------------------------
Full text: LICENSE-CLIENT.md

    web/
    desktop/
    mobile/
    streaming/
    krypto/
    plugins/
    packaging/
    Logo/
